#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:11 opt.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: opt.docbook:12 opt.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: opt.docbook:12 opt.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "options"
msgstr "opcions"

#. Tag: primary
#: opt.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "configuring &kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the documentation will show you how to configure &kword; to "
"suit your personal work style and preferences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; can be modified in three separate ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: opt.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: opt.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: opt.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Miscellaneous options"
msgstr "Opcions divèrsas"

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Key Bindings (keyboard shortcuts)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: opt.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "configuring keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: opt.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: opt.docbook:25 opt.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "changing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: opt.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "configuring key binding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: opt.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "keyboard key binding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure the keyboard shortcuts select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts... </guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:33 opt.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will bring up a dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit the shortcuts, the first thing you need to do is find the action you "
"want to edit. All of the possible actions are listed in the combo box "
"labeled <guilabel>Action</guilabel>. By using the scrollbar, locate the "
"action you are interested in and click once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected the action, you can turn your attention to the bottom "
"half of the dialog box. You use the bottom half of the dialog box to change "
"the shortcuts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "None"
msgstr "Pas cap"

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting this option, the currently selected action will not have any "
"keyboard shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default"
msgstr "Defaut"

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting this option, the currently selected action will use the default "
"shortcut. Once this option is clicked, the default keyboard shortcut is "
"listed below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom"
msgstr "Personalizat"

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting this option, you can choose any keyboard combination as a "
"shortcut for this action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defining custom keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You determine the key combination by clicking on the button with the current "
"keyboard combination in it. A second dialog will appear:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog box allows you to determine two different key combinations which "
"will trigger the desired action: <guilabel>Primary shortcut:</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Alternate shortcut:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defining simple keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Begin by deciding if you want to specify the <guilabel>Primary shortcut:</"
"guilabel> or <guilabel>Alternate shortcut:</guilabel> , by placing a mark in "
"the appropriate radiobutton."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"clearright.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> button will clear the "
"current keyboard shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now type the keyboard shortcut into the keyboard. &kword; will use this "
"keyboard combination as the new keyboard shortcut. The window will close "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:104 opt.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have completed your entries, simply click on <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> to accept the changes or <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to cancel "
"your changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defining multi-key keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Multi-key keyboard shortcuts can be used when you run out of simple keyboard "
"shortcuts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Multi-key shortcuts are edited the same as simple keyboard shortcuts, except "
"a mark is placed in the check box labeled <guilabel>Multi-key mode</"
"guilabel> <emphasis>prior</emphasis> to entering the keyboard shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now enter multiple keyboard characters for the keyboard shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is important to understand that keyboard <emphasis>combinations</"
"emphasis> (i.e.: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt; &Shift; <keycap>P</"
"keycap></keycombo>) are still a <emphasis>single character</emphasis> "
"because all the keys are depressed at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An example of a multi-key combination would be if you press <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Alt; <keycap>X</keycap></keycombo>, release both characters then "
"type a <keycap>W</keycap>. This is a multi-key combination."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Toolbars"
msgstr "Configurar las barras d'espleches"

#. Tag: primary
#: opt.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "configuring toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure &kword;'s toolbars select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a dialog box. You can add or remove as many toolbar "
"buttons to as many toolbars as you like. You can also move the buttons "
"around on the toolbar using this dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a button to a toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a button to a toolbar, you move it from the <guilabel>Available "
"actions:</guilabel> box to the <guilabel>Current actions:</guilabel> column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First select the toolbar you want to add a button to by selecting the "
"toolbar from the combo box labeled <guilabel>Toolbar:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now select the action you want to add from the combo box labeled "
"<guilabel>Available actions:</guilabel> by clicking once with the left mouse "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the blue arrow pointing to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:170 opt.docbook:193 opt.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button or the <guibutton>Apply</"
"guibutton> button has been clicked, the toolbars will change."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a button from a toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a button from a toolbar, you move it from the <guilabel>Current "
"actions:</guilabel> box to the <guilabel>Available actions:</guilabel> "
"column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First select the toolbar you want to delete a button from by selecting the "
"toolbar from the combo box labeled <guilabel>Toolbar:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the toolbar button you want to remove the button from the combo box "
"labeled <guilabel>Current actions:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the blue arrow pointing to the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving a button on a toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First select the toolbar you want to move a button on by selecting the "
"toolbar from the combo box labeled <guilabel>Toolbar:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To move a button, simply click on the button you want to move with the "
"<mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the up or down arrows to move the button up or down the toolbar "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure options regarding spelling and the user interface select "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kword;...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure &kword; User Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <guibutton>Interface</guibutton> will allow you to change the "
"following."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Units:"
msgstr "Unitats :"

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select your preferred unit of measurement. &kword; will use these units for "
"all measurements. See <link linkend=\"rulers\">Using Rulers</link> for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show status bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Placing a mark in this check box makes the status bar visible in &kword;. "
"See <link linkend=\"kword-screen\">The &kword; Screen</link> for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show scrollbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Placing a mark in this check box makes the scrollbar visible in &kword;. See "
"<link linkend=\"kword-screen\">The &kword; Screen</link> for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "PageUp/PageDown moves the caret"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this check box has a mark, then when you press the <keycap>PageUp</"
"keycap> and <keycap>PageDown</keycap> keys on the keyboard, &kword; moves "
"the text cursor (the caret) down one page. If there is no mark in this check "
"box then &kword; moves the view, but does not change the position of the "
"text cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of recent files:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This determines the maximum number of files that are listed under "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guisubmenu>Open Recent</guisubmenu></"
"menuchoice> command. You can adjust this value from 1-20."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid "Horizontal grid size:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Determines the horizontal size of the grid. When frames and tab stops are "
"placed on the page, they are placed on a point in the grid. This gives your "
"document a more professional look because elements are effectively aligned. "
"You can reduce the grid size if you need finer control of your layout."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vertical grid size:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Determines the vertical size of the grid. When frames are placed on the "
"page, they are placed on a point in the grid. This gives your document a "
"more professional look because elements are effectively aligned. You can "
"reduce the grid size if you need finer control of your layout."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Paragraph indent by toolbar buttons:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this spin box to determine how far the paragraph is indented when using "
"the increase indent button (<inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata "
"fileref=\"incindbut.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></"
"inlinemediaobject>) and the decrease indent button "
"(<inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"decindbut.png\" format="
"\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of pages per row in preview mode:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Determines the number of pages per row in preview mode. This determines the "
"size of the pages in preview mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:309 opt.docbook:429 opt.docbook:509 opt.docbook:531
#: opt.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are happy with the changes, simply click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:312 opt.docbook:432 opt.docbook:512 opt.docbook:534
#: opt.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>, all changes will be lost."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:315 opt.docbook:435 opt.docbook:515 opt.docbook:537
#: opt.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on the <guibutton>Defaults</guibutton> button restores all values "
"to their default values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure document options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default column spacing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this to adjust the default spacing between columns. For more information "
"on columns see <link linkend=\"columns\">Columns</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default font:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guibutton>Choose...</guibutton> button, and a new dialog will "
"appear. Use this dialog to choose the default font. This setting determines "
"the default font used by &kword; until further formatting is done. You can "
"revert any text to this default by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Default Format</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "Global language:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this drop down box to determine the default language for the document. "
"This setting is used by the hyphenation and spelling tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic hyphenation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place a mark in this checkbox if you want &kword; to automatically hyphenate "
"long words when it determines the word wrap in text frames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document settings"
msgstr "Paramètres de document"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autosave every (min):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this to adjust how often &kword; saves a temporary file. If you "
"set this value to <guilabel>No autosave</guilabel>, &kword; will not "
"autosave. You can adjust the autosave from 1 minute to 60 minutes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create backup file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is a mark in this checkbox, &kword; will automatically create a "
"backup file every time you save your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting page number:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this text box to determine the starting page number. For more "
"information on page numbering see <link linkend=\"page-number\">Page "
"Numbering</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is helpful if you have split a single document into multiple files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab stop:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each &kword; document has a default set of tab stops. If you add tab stops "
"to your document, the newly added tab stops override the default tabstops. "
"You can use this text box to define the spacing between default tab stops."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example. If you enter <userinput>1.5</userinput> in this text box, and "
"the unit of measure is in centimeters, then the first default tab stop will "
"be located 1.5 cm to the right of the left margin of the frame. The second "
"default tab stop will be located at 3 cm from the left margin, etc...."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cursor settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cursor in protected area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When there is a mark in this check box, and you click in a protected frame "
"of your document, a cursor appears. When the mark is removed from this check "
"box, and you click in a protected frame, there is no cursor visible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Spelling."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure the options for the speller, click on the button labeled "
"<guibutton>Spelling</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each option is detailed below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default language:"
msgstr "Lenga per defaut :"

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "Used by the spelling application to choose the correct dictionary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable background spellchecking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a mark is placed in this checkbox, &kword; will check the spelling of "
"words in your document as you type them. Words that &kword; believes are "
"misspelled will have a red line drawn under them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "Skip all uppercase words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a mark is placed in this checkbox, &kword; will not check the spelling of "
"any word which consists of all capital letters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is useful if the document you are working on uses a large number of "
"acronyms. If this box is left unchecked, most of those acronyms will be "
"incorrectly marked. By placing a mark in this checkbox, &kword; will not "
"mark the acronyms as misspelled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:478
#, no-c-format
msgid "Skip run-together words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this box is not checked, and &kword; finds a two words in its dictionary "
"that are placed next to each other, it will be marked as misspelled. If this "
"box is checked, the combined word will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Examples of such words are <emphasis>shutout</emphasis>, <emphasis>cannot</"
"emphasis>, and <emphasis>blackout</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checking this box will help prevent &kword; from flagging website and email "
"addresses for spelling errors. These addresses often contain words run "
"together."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignoring words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The bottom half of the dialog box allows you to designate specific words "
"(they may be specialized terminology, proper names, etc) which should be "
"ignored by the spelling program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a word to the ignore list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a word, type the word in the text box directly below the words "
"<guilabel>Ignore These Words</guilabel> and click the <guibutton>Add</"
"guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a word from the ignore list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove a word, select the word in the listbox containing all the "
"currently ignored words by clicking on it with the &LMB;. Now click the "
"<guibutton>Remove</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the order a word appears in the list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To move a word in the list, select the word in the listbox containing all "
"the currently ignored words by clicking on it with the &LMB;. Now click the "
"<guibutton>Move Up</guibutton> button or the <guibutton>Move Up</guibutton> "
"button to move the word within the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure formula options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:530
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this dialog to format the appearance of formulas in &kword;. See the "
"formula documentation for further details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure miscellaneous options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid "Misc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo/redo limit:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this spin box or slider to determine how many actions &kword; keeps in "
"its Undo buffer. Any action that exceeds this number will be forgotten."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display links"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Placing a mark in this check box makes document links visible in &kword;. If "
"there is no mark in this check box, document links will be hidden. See <link "
"linkend=\"links\">Document links</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid "Underline all links"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Placing a mark in this check box will have &kword; automatically underline a "
"document link when it is created. See <link linkend=\"links\">Document "
"links</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display comments"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Placing a mark in this check box makes document comments visible in &kword;. "
"See <link linkend=\"comments\">Document comments</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display field code"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is a mark in this check box, &kword; shows the variable name of "
"document variables, rather than the content of the variable in the &kword; "
"screen. If this check box does not have a mark, then &kword; shows the "
"contents of the variables."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option does not affect the printed output. The contents of the "
"variables are printed regardless of the state of this check box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "View Formatting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use these four check boxes to determine what formatting characters "
"are displayed when you have asked &kword; to <link linkend=\"view-formatting-"
"menu\">show formatting characters</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid "View formatting end paragraph"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggles the display of paragraph marks (new-line characters) on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid "View formatting space"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toggles the display of individual spaces on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid "View formatting tabs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toggles the display of tab stops on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: opt.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid "View formatting break"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toggles the display of frame breaks on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure path options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this dialog to set the <guilabel>Backup Path</guilabel> and the "
"directory for your <guilabel>Personal Expression</guilabel> in &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: opt.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Text-To-Speech options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: opt.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See the <link linkend=\"a11y-tts\">Text-to-Speech</link> section in the "
"accessibility chapter for further details."
msgstr ""
